{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/newton-physics/newton/pulls/3850","id":4234377250,"node_id":"PR_kwDOOdgpP878Y3gi","html_url":"https://github.com/newton-physics/newton/pull/3850","diff_url":"https://github.com/newton-physics/newton/pull/3850.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/newton-physics/newton/pull/3850.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/newton-physics/newton/issues/3850","number":3850,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add interaction support to ViewerViser","user":{"login":"eric-heiden","id":5869435,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4Njk0MzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5869435?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-heiden","html_url":"https://github.com/eric-heiden","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-heiden/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-heiden/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-heiden/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-heiden/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-heiden/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-heiden/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-heiden/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-heiden/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-heiden/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Description\n\nMake `ViewerViser` an interactive frontend for Newton examples: control the simulation, switch examples, manipulate gizmos, and apply picking forces from the browser.\n\n- Add native pause/step/reset, visualization and layer controls, example selection with loading feedback, and example-specific controls including held buttons.\n- Display live scalar plots and selectable camera-image streams. Reuse geometry and image buffers, avoid redundant transfers, and flush frame updates so stationary browser clients keep receiving animation.\n- Fix scene cleanup and colors on first reveal or after hidden updates, and keep recording timestamps monotonic across resets. Queue interactions on the simulation thread and discard events from removed handles or disconnected clients.\n- Require **Viser >=1.1.1** (locked to 1.1.1), install it in the `dev` extra for CI, use the supported line-thickness API, and expose the native Viser server for application-specific extensions.\n- Encode textured transparency in glTF materials, including updates to uniform batch opacity. Different opacities within one textured batch remain unsupported and produce an explicit warning; separate batches can use different opacities.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] New or existing tests cover these changes\n- [x] The documentation is up to date with these changes\n- [x] User-facing changes have [Towncrier fragments](https://github.com/newton-physics/newton/blob/main/changelog/README.md)\n\n## Test plan\n\n- **137 targeted viewer/example tests run, 3 skipped; all 25 Viser tests pass.** Replace fake-server/fake-picker tests with real Viser servers, WebSocket interactions, geometry/image/recording serialization, and CPU/CUDA force checks. Verify regression tests fail without their fixes.\n- **24 representative examples across all 16 example categories** exercised through Playwright/Chromium, covering rigid bodies, terrain, cloth, cables, soft bodies, particles, robotics, controllers, sensors, and coupled/multiple solvers. Check example switching, reset, pause/step, mouse picking, gizmos, layer visibility, held buttons, plots, image selection, stationary-camera animation, and recording playback.\n- The browser matrix used software WebGL with NVIDIA L4 simulation. A further **13-example interaction pass used NVIDIA-accelerated WebGL**, followed by focused browser checks after the cleanup. These cover force picking, gizmos, example switching, layer visibility, held buttons, plots, image selection, and transparent textured meshes.\n- `uvx pre-commit run -a`, API generation, and the Towncrier draft passed.\n\n## Bug fix\n\nA pick made after CUDA graph capture must still apply force. The picking kernel is now included during capture, with device-side state enabling and releasing the force during replay. Each layer uses its own picking state, and the multi-solver example binds each model before capture. This prevents drags that only move the browser handle or apply force to another model.\n\n## New feature / API change\n\n`ViewerViser` implements the existing gizmo, scalar, image, picking, and example-UI interfaces. `ViewerViser(paused=True)` and the read-only `server` property support initial pause state and native Viser extensions:\n\n```python\nimport warp as wp\nfrom newton.viewer import ViewerViser\n\nviewer = ViewerViser(paused=True)\nviewer.set_camera(wp.vec3(4.0, -3.0, 2.0), pitch=-22.0, yaw=143.0)\nwith viewer.server.gui.add_folder(\"Diagnostics\"):\n    viewer.server.gui.add_markdown(\"Application-specific status\")\n```\n\nThe example UI adapter supports a documented ImGui subset; use the native API for richer interfaces. The viewer owns the server. Native Viser callbacks run asynchronously; queue simulation changes for consumption before stepping.\n\n\n\n","created_at":"2026-08-08T11:38:04Z","updated_at":"2026-10-07T00:34:55Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"a8f6856eb768a5b1da090622a0db660f24b7fbd5","assignees":[{"login":"eric-heiden","id":5869435,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4Njk0MzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5869435?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-heiden","html_url":"https://github.com/eric-heiden","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-heiden/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-heiden/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-heiden/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-heiden/starred{/owner}{/repo}",